<statement>
<p>
	This program returns the winner of the current Tic-Tac-Toe game board matrix if one exists.
</p>

<tabular valign="top" top="minor">
	<col width="12%"/>
	<col width="88%"/>
	<row>
		<cell>Details:</cell>
		<cell><p>This program is your first helper function for the Tic-Tac-Toe game you will design in the following few homework assignments.</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>For example, the following game boards should not detect a winner:</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>However, these game boards would have a winner.</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>See class notes for how the game board state is defined.</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>You will want to use your</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>P32_matrix_sums</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row bottom="minor">
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>program from the previous assignment.</p></cell>
	</row>
</tabular>

<p>
	Examples:
<program>
	<code>
		winner = TTT41_winner_check_lastname([0 0 0; 0 1 0; 0 0 0])
		winner = 0
		winner = TTT41_winner_check_lastname([1 -1 -1; 0 1 -1; 1 0 -1])
		winner = -1
	</code>
</program>
</p>
</statement>
